window.docContents[137].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Bound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Bound":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh › Bound.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 128 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (10)def pqxdhKeyIndBounddef kemDecapsFailureTermdef activeIdCountdef activeSpkCountdef activeOpkCountdef activeSendCountdef activeSendOpkCountdef activeDhCountdef pqxdhKeyIndBoundActivetheorem pqxdhKeyIndBoundActive_le\n\n\n\nClosed-form handshake security bound for PQXDHTrusted: the statement. pqxdhKeyIndBoundActive (with activeIdCount, activeSpkCount, activeOpkCount, activeSendCount, activeSendOpkCount, activeDhCount) and Security.kemDecapsFailureTerm are used directly by the KeyInd and CLI security statements (Security/HeadlineDelta.lean, LibsignalCli/StatementPqElf.lean); the static pqxdhKeyIndBound is used by pqxdhAuthBound (Security/Auth/Game.lean) and pqxdhKeyIndBoundActive_le. The HNDL (-D KEM) bounds and deploymentSetup live in Computational/Proofs/SpecLemmas/SignalPqxdh/Bound.lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.pqxdhKeyIndBoundActive bounds the adversary's advantage in the multi-session PQXDH key-indistinguishability game (KeyInd1KeyRoAdvantage) in the classical -D DH regime where the handshake KDF (HkdfRO) is a random oracle, in terms of the online query budget q_on, Setup replication capacities, and handshake assumption advantages (Assumptions/Assumptions.lean). See Computational/docs/PQXDH.md for term-by-term derivations and numerical evaluation.\n\n\n\ndef pqxdhKeyIndBoundL40–54 ↗#Static-capacity upper bound on KeyInd advantage in the -D DH regime from the handshake assumption advantages (GapSigEufCma, KemShCr, GapDhWithSign; see DEV-PQ17) and Setup counts. The X25519 collision term sums 2^-250 per unordered pair over N_dh public keys and N_send_tot initiator dh2 values; the Kyber-1024 collision term sums 2^-255 over unordered N_spk_tot PQSPK pairs.\n\n\n\ndef kemDecapsFailureTermL58–61 ↗#KEM δ-correctness term: union bound of honest decapsulation failure (KemDeltaCorrect P δ) over (N_send_tot, N_spk_tot) session–pre-key pairs, scaled by the boolBias factor 2.\n\n\n\nActivity-bounded key-indistinguishability boundEach online KeyIndQuery S (isKeyIndOnlineQuery, excluding .roQuery) creates at most one honest principal, pre-key bundle, one-time pre-key, initiator session, and X25519 public key, so every active count is bounded by min q_on S.N_*.\n\ndef activeIdCountL71 ↗#\n\ndef activeSpkCountL73 ↗#\n\ndef activeOpkCountL75 ↗#\n\ndef activeSendCountL77 ↗#\n\ndef activeSendOpkCountL79 ↗#\n\ndef activeDhCountL81 ↗#\n\ndef pqxdhKeyIndBoundActiveL83–100 ↗#Activity-bounded upper bound on KeyInd advantage in the -D DH regime, obtained from pqxdhKeyIndBound by replacing static Setup capacities with min q_on S.N_*.\n\ntheorem pqxdhKeyIndBoundActive_leL102–126 ↗#The activity-bounded advantage bound is at most the static capacity bound.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/Bound.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Bound/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Bound"},"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementSession/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementSession":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session › StatementSession.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 180 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nLemma 2: Double Ratchet + SPQR V1 session securityTrusted: the statement. Read this file together with Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementComposed.lean, Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementIdsModel.lean, Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementSpkModel.lean, Computational/Specifications/Session/SpkHop2Red.lean, Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementPqOomFlag.lean, and LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalSpqrV1/KemFailFind.lean. The theorem session_secure (Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean) proves SessionSecure. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.SessionSecure is Lemma 2 of Formally Verifying Signal's Security Using AI (docs/PAPER_MAP.md): single-session security of the Triple Ratchet (Double Ratchet plus SPQR V1). It plays the real-or-random game SM.gameR (ACD19, Fig. 2) on sessionSchemeFixedSpk, with Bob's signed-pre-key coins s fixed and possibly known to the adversary, under configRefuseEarlyBobCorr. Quantified over a mixture oa : ProbComp α of session contexts (ida o, idb o, s o) and q-query adversaries A o, one costed reduction family D satisfying SessionCostedReductionFamilyBounded ℓ D bounds the mixed SM.gameR bias by sessionAdvantageBound + 2 * sessionKemFailProb whenever 2 * (q + 1) + 25002 < 2 ^ 32. Inside sessionAdvantageBound, prefixPrfAvg oa and prefixPrgAvg oa push oa into each reduction so the bound matches bhPrefixFullBoundMixV1With definitionally; α := Unit, oa := pure () recovers fixed-context security.Because SM.gameR lets the adversary supply send coins (including the ML-KEM-768 key-generation seed and encapsulation randomness in SPQR V1), the adversary can trigger ML-KEM decryption failure. The top-level term 2 * sessionKemFailProb (with factor 2 from |2 Pr - 1|) bounds this event in the game with A itself as twice the probability that some ordered pair of send tapes forms a failing exchange (MlKem.KemFailBad); evaluating it on A avoids reductions that could inflate the probability with a hard-coded failing pair. The game gameRCoinLogged runs oracleImplRM on smSchemeCoinLogged to record every send's coins in a WriterT log, and GameRCoinLoggedFaithful states that projecting out the game outcome recovers SM.gameR.\n\n\n\ndef sessionAdvantageBoundL65–93 ↗#Per-session Double Ratchet + SPQR V1 advantage bound for a context/adversary mixture oa : ProbComp α: uniformStartMixtureBound plus the leaked-pre-key hop-1, hop-3, and hop-2 terms on the costed reductions D.\n\nSend-coin-logged R-game and ML-KEM failure term\n\ndef smSchemeCoinLoggedL97–106 ↗#Monadic wrapper around sm over WriterT (List Coins) ProbComp that appends each send's coins r to the log and leaves receive unlogged.\n\ndef gameRCoinLoggedL108–123 ↗#Real-or-random game SM.gameR instrumented via smSchemeCoinLogged to return both the game outcome and the ordered list of coins for every honest or adversarial send that reaches sm.send (after cfg.sendOK, win, and epoch-management checks).\n\ndef GameRCoinLoggedFaithfulL125–133 ↗#Faithfulness of gameRCoinLogged: projecting to the Boolean outcome yields the exact distribution of SM.gameR.\n\ndef sessionKemFailProbL135–148 ↗#Probability, in gameRCoinLogged on sessionSchemeFixedSpk mixed over oa with adversaries A o, that some ordered pair of 64-byte SPQR V1 send tapes (coinBytes) triggers an ML-KEM decryption failure (K.KemFailBad).\n\ndef SessionSecureL150–181 ↗#Lemma 2 (Double Ratchet + SPQR V1 session security): existence of a bounded costed reduction family D such that, under the primitive, group, point-fiber (δ), and message-counter (2 * (q + 1) + 25002 < 2 ^ 32) hypotheses, every mixture oa of contexts (ida o, idb o, s o) and q-query adversaries A o has SM.gameR bias on sessionSchemeFixedSpk at most sessionAdvantageBound + 2 * sessionKemFailProb.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementSession.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementSession/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementSession"}});